.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NQCARD 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqcard ,
.Nm nqcardvrfy
.Nd make and check an identity card for a signing key
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqcard
.Fa "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen" "const char *name"
.Fa "const char *orcid" "const char *email" "const char *url"
.Fa "const char *affil" "int64_t created"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqcardvrfy
.Fa "const char *card" "size_t n" "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "nqcardf *f"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqcard
writes to
.Fa out ,
of
.Fa cap
bytes, an identity card
.Pq Ql noqtis-idcard-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5
in canonical JSON: the public key
.Fa pk
of
.Fa alg
with
.Fa name
and, when not
.Dv NULL ,
.Fa orcid ,
.Fa email ,
.Fa url
and
.Fa affil ,
made at
.Fa created
(seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z) and signed by
.Fa sk
under the context
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1 .
.Fa *outlen
gets the card's size, also when
.Fa cap
is too small.
The signature is verified before the card is written.
.Pp
The fields, in bytes:
.Fa name
and
.Fa affil
are 1 to 255 bytes of UTF-8 with no control character (C0, DEL or C1)
and no space at either end;
.Fa orcid
is an ORCID iD,
.Ql 0000-0002-1825-0097 ,
or its
.Ql https://orcid.org/
address, whose last character is its ISO 7064 MOD 11-2 check digit
.Pq Ql X No for 10 ,
a lower-case
.Ql x
taken as
.Ql X ;
the card holds the bare iD.
.Fa email
is
.Ql local@domain.tld ,
at most
.Dv NQCARDEMAIL
(254) bytes;
.Fa url
an
.Ql https://
address with a host, at most
.Dv NQCARDURL
(1024) bytes; neither has a space or a control character.
The arguments and fields are checked before the algorithm, so a call
refused for a field returns
.Er NQEARG
whatever
.Fa alg
is.
.Pp
.Fn nqcardvrfy
checks the
.Fa n
bytes at
.Fa card
(at most
.Dv NQCARDMAX ,
256 KiB): it must be a
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1
card in canonical form, with exactly its members, fields within the
limits above (the ORCID iD bare, its check digit right), a post-quantum
algorithm, a key and a signature of that algorithm's sizes, and a
signature that verifies under the key it carries with the context
.Ql noqtis-idcard-1 .
With
.Fa pk
not
.Dv NULL ,
the card's key must also be
.Fa pk ,
of
.Fa pklen
bytes.
On success
.Fa *f
gets the card:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct {
  nqsalg alg;
  uint8_t pk[NQCARDPK];   /* the card's public key, pklen bytes */
  size_t pklen;
  uint8_t fp[32];         /* its SHA-256 (nqinsp's info.key) */
  int64_t created;        /* seconds since 1970, UTC */
  char utc[21];           /* the same, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ */
  char name[256];
  char orcid[20];         /* "" for a field the card has not */
  char email[NQCARDEMAIL + 1];
  char url[NQCARDURL + 1];
  char affil[256];
} nqcardf;
.Ed
.Pp
On any other result
.Fa *f
is zeroed.
A card is self-signed: a card that verifies was written by whoever holds
its key and is unchanged, which does not make the name true; compare
.Fa fp
with the one its holder published, or pin
.Fa pk .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Dv NQOK
The card was written, or it verifies.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fn nqcard :
the algorithm is not a post-quantum signature (Ed25519 alone).
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A
.Dv NULL
argument, a field out of its limits, keys of the wrong sizes or not a
pair, or
.Fa created
before 1970 or after 9999.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
.Fn nqcardvrfy :
the signature does not verify, or the card is not for
.Fa pk .
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
.Fn nqcardvrfy :
not a card as above.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fn nqcardvrfy :
more than
.Dv NQCARDMAX
bytes.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation hook returned
.Dv NULL .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-idcard 1 ,
.Xr nqinsp 3 ,
.Xr nqkstmt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
